  "title": "The depth of a charge hole is the toggle width",
  "subject": "How many distinctions linear local reasoning must hold to refute an impossible charge network",
  "conclusion": "Over a field that cannot compute in the charge group, linear local reasoning refutes an impossible charge network exactly once it holds as many distinctions as the graph's toggle width, whatever the charges, while matched rings need one knot. On cubic graphs with up to 10 vertices this depth is cutwidth + 1, and it is not a function of treewidth.",
